**Overview**: How to configure a cert-manager Certificate so its Secret is automatically replicated to other namespaces using `kubernetes-replicator` (Mittwald/Stakater-style).

- **Scope**: instructions for adding a replicated TLS Secret to new namespaces, using `spec.secretTemplate` on `Certificate` (recommended), push-based annotations, and quick manual alternatives.

**Install Replicator**: - : Install the replicator operator (Mittwald or Stakater) in the cluster. Example (Helm):

- **Helm**: `helm repo add mittwald https://helm.mittwald.de && helm repo update`
- **Install**: `helm upgrade --install kubernetes-replicator mittwald/kubernetes-replicator --namespace replicator --create-namespace`

**Recommended (automatic)**: use `secretTemplate` in the `Certificate` so cert-manager creates the Secret with the replicator annotation.

- **Edit Certificate**: add `spec.secretTemplate.annotations` to the Certificate. Example `cert-manager/wildcard-certificate.yaml`:

  apiVersion: cert-manager.io/v1
  kind: Certificate
  metadata:
    name: wildcard-enricocc-tls
    namespace: cert-manager
  spec:
    secretName: wildcard-enricocc-tls
    secretTemplate:
      annotations:
        replicator.v1.mittwald.de/replicate-to: "adguard,cattle-system"
    issuerRef:
      name: letsencrypt-dns01-cloudflare
      kind: ClusterIssuer
    commonName: "*.enricocc.com"
    dnsNames:
      - "*.enricocc.com"
      - enricocc.com

- **Apply**: `kubectl apply -f cert-manager/wildcard-certificate.yaml`

**If the Secret already exists** (no downtime approach)

- **Annotate existing Secret** (push the replication immediately):
  - `kubectl -n cert-manager annotate secret wildcard-enricocc-tls replicator.v1.mittwald.de/replicate-to="adguard,cattle-system" --overwrite`
- **Verify replication**:
  - `kubectl -n adguard get secret wildcard-enricocc-tls -o yaml`
  - `kubectl -n cattle-system get secret wildcard-enricocc-tls -o yaml`

**If you want cert-manager to recreate the Secret with the template**

- **Delete source Secret** (cert-manager will recreate it):
  - `kubectl -n cert-manager delete secret wildcard-enricocc-tls`
  - then verify: `kubectl -n cert-manager get secret wildcard-enricocc-tls -o yaml`

**Pull-based alternative** (create empty target Secret that pulls from source)

- In the target namespace create a Secret with the annotation `replicator.v1.mittwald.de/replicate-from: cert-manager/wildcard-enricocc-tls` and empty data keys for TLS secrets. Example:

  apiVersion: v1
  kind: Secret
  metadata:
    name: wildcard-enricocc-tls
    namespace: adguard
    annotations:
      replicator.v1.mittwald.de/replicate-from: cert-manager/wildcard-enricocc-tls
  type: kubernetes.io/tls
  data:
    tls.crt: ""
    tls.key: ""

**Special cases & tips**

- **TLS secret format**: ensure `type: kubernetes.io/tls` and keys `tls.crt` and `tls.key` exist (may be empty for pull-based).
- **Strip labels**: to avoid other operators deleting replicated secrets (e.g., Strimzi) add `replicator.v1.mittwald.de/strip-labels: "true"` on source.
- **OwnerReferences**: replicator removes ownerReferences by default; to keep them set `replicator.v1.mittwald.de/keep-owner-references: "true"`.
- **Rene wal / Renewal**: when cert-manager renews the source secret, the replicator will update targets automatically.
- **RBAC**: replicator requires read on source namespace and create/update on target namespaces. Verify clusterrole/serviceaccount values if install fails.
- **Image pull issues**: if operator pods show `ImagePullBackOff`, mirror the operator image to an internal registry and update `image.repository`/`image.tag` or add `imagePullSecrets`.

**Quick troubleshooting**

- **Replicator logs**: `kubectl -n replicator logs deployment/kubernetes-replicator -f`
- **Check annotations on source**: `kubectl -n cert-manager get secret wildcard-enricocc-tls -o yaml`
- **Check if target exists**: `kubectl -n <target> get secret wildcard-enricocc-tls -o yaml`
- **Ingress check**: confirm `secretName` in Ingress and controller logs if TLS not served:
  - `kubectl -n <ingress-namespace> describe ingress <ingress-name>`
  - `kubectl -n ingress-nginx logs -l app.kubernetes.io/name=ingress-nginx -f`

**Where to edit**

- Add/modify `cert-manager/wildcard-certificate.yaml` and apply, or use `kubectl patch` to add `secretTemplate` without downtime.

**Cleanup**

- If you created a temporary Job or manual resources for the annotation, remove them once the replication is working: `kubectl -n replicator delete job replicate-wildcard-annotation` and remove temp YAML files from the repo.

